# Gen1 PRM prototype scratch: the generated corpora and the two
# 255-266MB ASCII weight dumps are artefacts, regenerated by
# generation_1/I1/gen_data_gen1.py and the trainers; they are not
# repository content. Models ship as release assets, never as tree files.
#
# This used to be a single directory-wide rule (`generation_1/`), and that rule
# also excluded the Python harnesses that generate and score those artefacts:
# run_big.py, run_tests_gen1.py, algos_gen1_ext.py, algos_gen1_big.py,
# gen_data_gen1.py and MODEL_CARD_GEN1.md are source, and they were absent from
# every commit and push while the 266MB dump they were written beside was the
# whole reason the rule existed. A directory-wide exclude is easier to type
# than a list of what not to keep, and the cost is that the audit trail for a
# harness disappears along with its scratch space. Excluded by name now.
# The paths carry the I1/ subdirectory since the 2026-10-19 I1/I2 restructure
# (heritage -> I1, conglomeration -> I2); the old top-level names are kept as
# history since HEAD still carries those paths.
generation_1/I1/corpus/
generation_1/I1/results/
generation_1/I1/results_big/
generation_1/I1/gen1_model.txt
generation_1/corpus/
generation_1/results/
generation_1/results_big/
generation_1/gen1_model.txt
generation_1/**/__pycache__/
generation_1/__pycache__/
generation_1/I3/corpus/model_i3.txt
# I4 (fire-risk): sources/specs/cards/results-metrics are tracked; the 157MB
# corpus, 172MB raw feature data, ASCII weight dump, checkpoints and
# probability dumps are reproducible outputs and live outside history.
generation_1/I4/corpus/*
generation_1/I4/data/
generation_1/I4/models/i4/
generation_1/I4/results/*.bin
generation_1/I4/results/*.npy
# Small artifacts the I4 card lists as evidence stay tracked beside the
# ignored roots they live under.
!generation_1/I4/corpus/qc.json
!generation_1/I4/corpus/corpus.hdr
!generation_1/I4/corpus/feature_manifest.json
!generation_1/I4/corpus/metadata.json

# 243-BDC (cloned I4 + I5 generations + Idea1/LDFD tracks): large data,
# models, results, and figures are reproducible outputs / external artefacts
# and live outside history. Source configs, specs, cards, and READMEs remain
# tracked per the 243-BDC README.
243-BDC/I4/corpus/*
243-BDC/I4/data/
243-BDC/I4/models/i4/
243-BDC/I4/results/*.bin
243-BDC/I4/results/*.npy
243-BDC/I5/corpus/*
243-BDC/I5/models/*.lancius
243-BDC/I5/results_big/*
243-BDC/data/raw/*
243-BDC/data/processed/*
243-BDC/models/*
243-BDC/results/*
243-BDC/figures/*
243-BDC/literature/*
# Small artifacts stay tracked beside the ignored roots they live under.
!243-BDC/I4/corpus/qc.json
!243-BDC/I4/corpus/corpus.hdr
!243-BDC/I4/corpus/feature_manifest.json
!243-BDC/I4/corpus/metadata.json
!243-BDC/I5/gen1_mu_sd.txt
!243-BDC/I5/README.md
!243-BDC/I5/paths.py
!243-BDC/I5/run_big_i5.py
!243-BDC/README.md
!243-BDC/experiment_log.md
!243-BDC/configs/
!243-BDC/src/
!243-BDC/tests/
!243-BDC/requirements.txt

